Day 1 - HTML Document Structure
  Html is Hypertext markup language. It tells the web browser how to structure the website.
  a basic HTML structure contains:
'<!DOCTYPE html>'- tells the browser uses HTML5
  '<html>'- contains the whole html document
  '<head>'- contains information about the page such as page title
  '<body>'- contains the content of the web page seen by users.
  Elements in Html often have an opening tag and closing tag.
